(Examination Procedures and Rules) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(ABOUT THIS DOCUMENT) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(SAMPLE / DUMMY DOCUMENT for testing only. Not real university policy.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(EXAMINATION SCHEDULE AND HALL TICKET) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The examination department publishes the schedule on the notice board and the student) Tj T*
(portal at least 14 days before the exams. Students must collect their hall ticket from the) Tj T*
(examination department \(Main Block, first floor\) three days before the first exam. A) Tj T*
(student without a hall ticket and a valid college ID card will not be allowed into the) Tj T*
(examination hall.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(CONDUCT INSIDE THE HALL) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Students must reach the hall 20 minutes before the start time. Mobile phones, smart) Tj T*
(watches and notes are strictly prohibited. Any student found using unfair means will be) Tj T*
(reported to the discipline committee, and the paper may be cancelled.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(ATTENDANCE REQUIREMENT) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A minimum of 75 percent attendance in every subject is required to appear in the end-) Tj T*
(semester examination. Students with shortage of attendance may apply to the head of) Tj T*
(department for condonation with a valid medical certificate.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(RESULTS AND RE-EVALUATION) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Results are declared within 30 days after the last exam. A student may apply for re-) Tj T*
(evaluation within 7 days of the result declaration by submitting the re-evaluation form) Tj T*
(and the prescribed fee at the examination department. Revised marks are final.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(CERTIFICATES AND TRANSCRIPTS) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Provisional certificates and transcripts can be requested at the examination department) Tj T*
(with a written application. Processing normally takes 10 working days.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
